@subsection types.h / types.c

@defun llines_record_hash (PyObject* obj) @arrow{} Py_hash_t
We need a hash for the RECORD.  We would like the hash to be the same
even if the RECORD gets flushed and read back in at a different
location... (which I don't think can happen because we should be
holding a reference to the RECORD..., but just in case...).  So, we
use the RECORD's key.  And rather than design a new hash, we just use
Python's string hash.
@end defun

@defun llines_record_richcompare (PyObject *self, PyObject *other, int op) @arrow{} PyObject*
Sorting rules -- RECORDS < NODES < everything else.

For comparisons between two RECORDS, major sort on record type, minor
sort on keynum.
@end defun

@defun llines_node_richcompare (PyObject *self, PyObject *other, int op) @arrow{} PyObject*
Sorting rules -- RECORDS < NODES < everything else.

For comparisons between two NODES, first determine the type and key of
the records containing the nodes, then major sort on record type, minor
sort on keynum.

This, obviously, ``fails'' when one or both nodes is a detached node
or both nodes are part of the same record.
@end defun

